Accumulate the alphabetic run across tokens. When a new token continues it,
predict a negative response if the joined string is a familiar English word,
particularly after a newline or without a space in the initial token.
Case and the number of pieces adjust the response. Other positions stay near
zero. Familiarity means corpus-based Zipf frequency from wordfreq; this is a
broad orthographic approximation, not a list of token-specific exceptions.
