The tokenizer keeps many long runs of one character as a single token: "................",
"^^^^", "████", "--------", or a long run of spaces. Indentation made of no-break spaces
(" \xa0 \xa0") is kept the same way. When such a token repeats the token just before it,
the text is continuing a run, and this component goes strongly negative: about -10 for
runs of four or more characters, -5 for two or three. If the previous token was the same
character in a different length (the run's token changed, as in "________" then "____"),
it is mildly negative (-2.5). A literal escaped tab (the two characters backslash-t,
common in code strings) repeated right after itself ("\\t\\t") is about -3.
Everything else is 0.
