component writes into the residual stream at that position. Rules, strongest first:

1. "the" glued to a preceding word piece (no space in front, as when the tokenizer
   splits a longer word, e.g. "Gö|the", "ver|the|ilen"): 3.9 for exactly "the";
   1.8 for other pieces that contain "the" (ther, ithe, ethe); 0.5 for a piece that
   only contains "th" (ath, eth, oth).
2. Capitalised "The" in the middle of a text (inside a title or name, or after a quote,
   bracket or colon): 1.0. After a newline: 0.5.
   At the start of a sentence (after . ! ?): -0.1.
3. A lowercase " the" that is its own word:
   0.9 after an opening bracket, quote or colon;
   0.8 after is/was/are/were/be/been/have/has/had/all/'s;
   0.2 by default (after of, to, by, for, with, and, comma, ...);
   0.0 after in, on, that, into, from, between, at, if, through, before, after;
   -0.3 after about, within, under, during, using, than, because, and after
   verbs such as find, calculate, reduce, determine, understand.
4. A doubled middle dot "··" (a run of dot leaders in a long document): -1.4.
5. Everything else: 0.

Variance explained is about 0.19 on held-out eval rows. Most of the rest is
spread over many tokens with small values, and over rare large spikes.
"""

READS = ()

AUX = {" is", " was", " are", " were", " be", " been", " being", " has", " have", " had",
       " all", "'s", " having", " get", " made"}
NEG = {" about", " within", " under", " during", " using", " than", " because", " including",
       " inside", " along", " near", " how", " reduce", " calculate", " find", " determine",
       " understand", " improve", " affect", " set", " compute", " check", " write",
       " increase", " represent", " follow", " create", " know", " use", " contains"}
ZERO = {" in", " on", " that", " into", " from", " between", " if", " If", " since", " In",
        " At", " at", " through", " before", " after", " while", " when", " where", " until",
        " over", " across"}


def step(carry, prefix, upstream):
    cur = prefix.token_strings[-1]
    prev = prefix.token_strings[-2] if len(prefix) > 1 else ""
    word = cur.strip().lower()
    glued = not cur.startswith(" ") and prev[-1:].isalpha()

    if glued and "the" in word:
        return None, 3.9 if word == "the" else 1.8
    if glued and "th" in word:
        return None, 0.5
    if cur.strip() == "··":
        return None, -1.4
    if word != "the":
        return None, 0.0

    end = prev.rstrip(" ")[-1:]  # last character before this token
    if cur.strip() != "the":  # capitalised "The"
        if end in ("", ".", "!", "?"):
