"""A val/wal spelling detector, sensitive to token and word boundaries.

The strongest negative responses are equivalence words and fragments that
complete a val/wal syllable inside a word. Whole, familiar words such as
'value' and 'interval' respond much less. Transliteration extends the same
rules to other scripts. Completions like vist/vost and German welt have
positive responses instead. A small offset models document openings.
This is a coarse spelling rule, not a semantic equivalence test.
